load @term/seed/structure/set
  find set

# A category: objects and the morphisms (arrows) between them, with morphisms that compose associatively and an
# identity arrow on every object. A category is the mathematics of structure-and-structure-preserving-map in the
# abstract, the same shape whether the objects are sets, groups, spaces, or types. Functors map between categories and
# natural transformations map between functors. The form carries the collection of objects and the collection of
# morphisms; the composition and identity laws are the axioms.
form category
  link objects, like set
  link morphisms, like set
